# SQL's uppercase `LIMIT`: DS0105. `limit` itself is accepted.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | LIMIT 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..29
  PIPELINE@0..28
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    TAKE_OP@20..28
      IDENT@20..25 "LIMIT"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      LITERAL@26..28
        LONG@26..28 "10"
  WHITESPACE@28..29 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `LIMIT` is not an operator
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | LIMIT 10
  |                     ^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: operator names are lowercase: write `limit`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | limit 10
which parses without errors
